From 83ab8f801ccd0fdf5b702a567202ebf9c5d5f532 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: DeltaVector1 <DeltaVector1@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 7 Aug 2026 04:26:49 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 21/36] Add the glm52-ops skill; make the watchdog tests drive
 the real scripts

Turn the repeated operations into a Prime Agent skill and fix three faults
that the work exposed.

The skill (.agents/skills/glm52-ops) holds status, reward, watch, tunnels,
engines, alive, repair, deploy, start and stop. It puts four rules into code
and raises Refused rather than obey a request that breaks them: n79 is never
touched, PRIME_BATCH_CACHE is never forwarded, watch blocks instead of running
in the background, and reward gives no trend verdict below 10 steps or inside
twice the residual spread. reward also separates the effective series from the
all series, because a falling error rate lifts `all` without the model
learning anything.

watchdog_smoketest.sh re-implemented each watchdog's decision and tested the
copy. It reported 18 of 18 while three cases asserted the opposite of the
shipped behaviour: they still expected the tunnel watchdog to refuse to
rebuild on mass failure, a rule removed after it froze the run for 5 hours. It
now shadows curl, ss, kill, sudo, docker and sleep on PATH and drives the real
scripts. 26 tests. Verified by restoring the removed rule, which turns 4 red.

tunnel_watchdog.sh logged only when it killed a port, so a healthy idle
watchdog and a wedged one looked identical. It now writes a heartbeat.

A liveness probe must not match its own command line. pgrep -fc counts its own
grep; pgrep -f "bash .*name.sh" over ssh matches the remote shell, because the
shell really is bash and .* joins it to the name. Bracketing the first word
does not help. Bracket the last token. Putting a pkill and a start in one ssh
command killed all three watchdogs on 2026-08-07.

engine_watchdog.sh takes START, RELOAD_TRIES and RELOAD_WAIT from the
environment so the suite can drive it.

Docs: AGENTS.md rewritten current and short, since it loads every session; it
still described global expert parallelism and cp=4, which the run does not
use. Measurements moved to docs/PERFORMANCE.md, marked by topology era. The
startup order was written three ways in three documents; the correct rule has
two cases and is now stated once. Judge port corrected to 26406.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_017wiESxhziDrnsLnG9aizTd
